// "Lagon Duvet": a tropical lagoon at the foot of a jungle cliff (issue #20, the special
// environments' circuit), redrawn after the guide « Conception des circuits » (issue #150,
// docs/GAME_DESIGN.md § 16). Original layout, about 1820 m a lap, turning right: the start
// straight on the cliff top, 10 m up, ends on the glide ramp; the glider flies over the lagoon
// (a gap with no road) and lands on the north beach; a hairpin to the right on the beach, then
// the road dives into the lagoon and runs under its water before coming out of it; a hairpin to
// the left at the foot of the jungle cliff, and the climb north up its face, in anti-gravity, to
// the summit, 46 m up, high over the beach; a hairpin to the right round the summit, the way down
// south (in anti-gravity) and a drop; the summit's chicane (a tight corner to the left, then one
// to the right); the serpent down the east slope (a hairpin to the left, one to the right); the
// risky jump's corner (a tight corner to the right, its inside a drop, that a ramp crosses), its
// wide landing, west; the bulge round a giant palm, whose hidden road runs straight behind a
// curtain of lianas; the last corner, that the grass bridge crosses behind a panel that breaks
// under a boost. Five hairpins of 180° (a Normal bot drifts them), the bulge's S (right 150°
// between two left 75°), the chicane and three more tight corners of 90°: no long soft curve,
// one long straight (the start straight and the glide). The pieces of the shortcuts (the jump's
// corner and its landing; the bulge, the last corner and their paths) are the Forêt Frimousse's
// (the Corniche Cannelle's, issues #107, #156: their gains and their hiding were tuned), with
// other covers; the glide is the Lagon's own (issue #20); the rest is new.
//
// Drawn as a plan of straights and arcs, its points every 8 m along it (the parameters below
// follow them).
//
// Format: see src/track/data.rs. Point 0 is the start line; karts drive toward point 1 (north,
// -Z), then turn right. The grid sits on the straight behind point 0.
(
    name: "Lagon Duvet",
    // Dressing (issue #11): the lagoon (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), the same every time (seed),
    // and pieces placed by hand: checkered flags at the start line, a wreck on the north beach,
    // beyond the hairpin, and a lookout tower out of it, a giant palm that hides the hidden road,
    // an obelisk by the jump's corner.
    biome: "Lagon",
    // Issue #104: its music (`assets/data/music.ron`).
    music: "joyful-jungle",
    decor_seed: 20,
    // Issue #150: the lagoon's terrain (`assets/data/biomes.ron`: jungle cliffs in steps), and it
    // hugs the road (`embank`, rise over run: about 31°, as on the circuits of issue #211): the
    // climb up the cliff, the summit and the serpent down the east slope are carried by the cliff
    // up to their walls, instead of skirts down to the beach. The voids stay (the jump's corner,
    // the bulge, the last corner: 6 m under the road at least); the lagoon keeps its ground.
    terrain: (height: 52.0, scale: 130.0, cliffs: 0.6, terrace: 12.0, floor: 0.2,
              rock: (0.50, 0.46, 0.40), steep: 0.9, embank: 0.6),
    props: [
        (model: "racing-kit/flagCheckers", at: 0.0, side: Both, height: 4.0, radius: 0.9, gap: 1.8),
        (model: "pirate-kit/ship-wreck", at: 32.000, side: Left, height: 8.0, radius: 6.0, gap: 6.0, yaw: -20.0),
        (model: "pirate-kit/tower-complete-small", at: 39.500, side: Left, height: 8.0, radius: 2.4, gap: 1.5),
        (model: "nature-kit/tree_palmDetailedTall", at: 202.216, side: Right, height: 24.0, radius: 3.8, gap: 8.0),
        (model: "nature-kit/statue_obelisk", at: 178.204, side: Left, height: 16.0, radius: 3.0, gap: 2.0),
    ],
    checkpoint_spacing: 25.0,
    points: [
